    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0167" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/6–2550: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-26T05:00:00+10:00">June 26, 1950—5 a.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 25—3:46 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>944. Sent CINCFE; repeated information
                    Department 944. President has not yet left Seoul (remytel 940, June 26). He has
                    just phoned that he was unable to get through to General MacArthur or to his
                    Chief of Staff<anchor n="1" xml:id="d80-f1"/> in order to submit an urgent
                    request that 10 F–51s with bombs and bazookas be delivered to Taegu where Korean
                    pilots are awaiting to take off. He hopes that they can be here before dawn. He
                    asserts that unless these planes are here before dawn, it will be very difficult
                    to meet the northern attack.</p>
                <pb facs="0168" n="148" xml:id="pg148"/>
                <p>In addition, he requests 36 105 mm. howitzers, 36 75 mm. anti-tank guns, and 36
                    155 mm. howitzers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d80-f1" n="1" xml:id="d80-f1-content">
